## 3️⃣ Area 3: Casino & Betting Core Features## 📋 Testing Structure

* Asynchronous Stream Analysis: Isolate active WebSocket connection states. Separate transactional betting frames from background interface polling activities.
* Time-Slice Capture: Isolate sports betting frames down to fractions of a second. Target the exact window when an athletic play concludes but before the server sets the betting line to suspended status.
* Injection Surface Tracking: Document every text block that displays text back to administrative operators or general chat rooms.

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Odds/Multiplier Tampering Confirmation: Check bet receipts. A vulnerability is confirmed if modifying outgoing WebSocket strings properties causes the resulting bet validation receipt to register high odds values or high multiplier variables that do not match the real-time baseline rules.
* Client-Side Validation Flaw Confirmation: Check state dependencies. A vulnerability exists if arbitrary text properties or outcome fields (like forced success markers) sent from your computer dictate win payouts directly, rather than relying on server-side logic calculations.
* XSS Execution Confirmation: Look for unauthorized out-of-band communication. A vulnerability is confirmed when your out-of-band interaction log captures a connection from a corporate domain containing information like page locations, internal tokens, or user cookies.

------------------------------
## 4️⃣ Area 4: Infrastructure & Input Handling## 📋 Testing Structure

* Blind Interaction Auditing: Use unique out-of-band domain tokens for every individual query box to trace exactly which field triggers external network traffic.
* KYC Document Structure Manipulation: Inject payloads directly inside standard document file properties without altering structural components (like magic bytes or header components) to prevent basic validation filters from blocking them.
* Safe Traversal Tracking: Look only for safe system configurations (like system hostnames or local path structures) to prove vulnerabilities like file access or command execution without downloading sensitive target data.

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* SSRF Confirmation: Review DNS/HTTP logs. A vulnerability is confirmed if an internal system router reaches out to your tracking server or returns internal data blocks (like AWS metadata strings) inside its standard server response body.
* XXE / LFR Confirmation: Inspect response output files. A vulnerability is confirmed if a file upload result returns explicit configuration strings (like text blocks matching system password file styles or localized machine information).
* RCE Confirmation: Check command feedback loops. A vulnerability is confirmed if the target system returns explicit system command text output (such as current system identity responses) directly within page text blocks or within raw headers.

